# Sources layered onto --base, in order, when no --pr/--patch is given.
#
#   pr:<n>        siderolabs/talos pull request, fetched at build time
#   patch:<file>  path relative to this file
#
# Prefer pr: over vendoring. A PR that is already open needs no copy here, and
# a copy silently goes stale the moment the PR is updated. Vendor a patch only
# for work that exists nowhere upstream yet.
#
# Each source is dropped from this file once it lands in --base; the script
# says so when a source is already present. When this file is empty, the whole
# custom-media path retires in favour of stock upstream images.

# LVM physical volumes must be created on the decrypted mapper, not the LUKS
# ciphertext. Without it the volume group forms on the ciphertext and the
# volume then fails permanently with "lvm2-pv != luks".
pr:14145

# Deactivate an LVM volume group before closing the LUKS mapper underneath it,
# so shutdown does not stall on "mapped device is still in use". Not upstream
# in any form yet -- open a PR and replace this with a pr: line.
patch:0001-lvm-deactivation-controller.patch

# vgextend is given every desired device rather than only the ones missing from
# the group, because the spec names PVs by kernel device (/dev/dm-0) while the
# PV status reports the mapper alias (/dev/mapper/luks2-r-lvm0). LVM refuses the
# whole command when any device in it is already a member, and the refusal is
# swallowed as ErrExists -- so a volume group stops one PV short and spins
# forever. Order-dependent, so it presents as intermittent. Not upstream.
patch:patches/talos/0002-lvm-vgextend-only-missing-devices.patch
